-Su,PH 10:00-18:00","wp":"ja:神戸海洋博物館","ds":"Kobe Maritime Museum is a museum in Kobe, Japan focusing on the history of Japanese shipping and Kobe harbor. One of the former exhibits is the Yamato 1 removed in 2016 along with the TSL Hayate.","wpu":"Kobe Maritime Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Kobe_Maritime_Museum-A_bird%27s-eye_view_from_Kobe_Port_Tower.jpg/960px-Kobe_Maritime_Museum-A_bird%27s-eye_view_from_Kobe_Port_Tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Kobe Port Emigrants","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":34.68149,"lo":135.18947,"d":174},{"n":"Kawasaki World","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":34.682924,"lo":135.188031,"d":180,"h":"Mo-Su,PH 10:00-18:00","wp":"ja:カワサキワールド"},{"n":"Kobe Port Tower","g":"sights","k":"viewpoint","la":34.682628,"lo":135.186724,"d":302,"w":"https://www.kobe-port-tower.com/","wp":"ja:神戸ポートタワー","ds":"The Kobe Port Tower (神戸ポートタワー, Kōbe Pōto Tawā) is a landmark in the port city of Kobe, Japan. The sightseeing tower was completed in 1963 and was temporarily closed from late 2009 to 28 April 2010 and again from 27 September 2021 to 26 April 2024 for renovation. It is located in Chuo-ku, Kobe, Hyōgo Prefecture, Japan.","wpu":"Kobe Port Tower","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/20190901_Kobe_Port_Tower-1.jpg/960px-20190901_Kobe_Port_Tower-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"アトア","g":"sights","k":"aquarium","la":34.683244,"lo":135.19361,"d":331,"w":"https://atoa-kobe.jp/"},{"n":"Kobe Overseas Chinese History Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":34.685991,"lo":135.187165,"d":421,"wp":"ja:神戸華僑歴史博物館"},{"n":"戦没した船と海員の資料館","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":34.68589,"lo":135.186615,"d":446,"wp":"ja:戦没した船と海員の資料館"},{"n":"Kobe City Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":34.687282,"lo":135.192926,"d":546,"wp":"ja:神戸市立博物館","ds":"The Kobe City Museum (神戸市立博物館, Kōbe-shiritsu Hakubutsukan) opened in Kobe, Japan in 1982. It is one of Japan's many museums which are supported by a municipality. The museum resulted from the merger of the Municipal Archaeological Art Museum and Municipal Namban Art Museum.","wpu":"Kobe City Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Kobe_city_museum01_1920.jpg/960px-Kobe_city_museum01_1920.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Nankinmachi","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":34.68799,"lo":135.188079,"d":581,"w":"http://nankinmachi.or.jp/","wp":"ja:南京町 (神戸市)"},{"n":"蝶屋","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":34.687886,"lo":135.187596,"d":586},{"n":"Xian Gate","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":34.687744,"lo":135.186769,"d":604},{"n":"南京町広場","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":34.688217,"lo":135.188122,"d":604},{"n":"Kobe Lamp Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":34.688221,"lo":135.194129,"d":692,"wp":"ja:神戸らんぷミュージアム"},{"n":"KOBEとんぼ玉ミュージアム","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":34.68858,"lo":135.19377,"d":709,"w":"https://www.lampwork-museum.com","wp":"ja:KOBEとんぼ玉ミュージアム","ds":"Kobe , officially Kobe City (神戸市, Kōbe-shi; [koː.beꜜ.ɕi]), is the capital city of Hyōgo Prefecture, Japan. With a population of around 1.5 million, Kobe is Japan's seventh-largest city and the third-largest port city after Tokyo and Yokohama. It is located in the Kansai region, which makes up the southern side of the main island of Honshū, on the north shore of Osaka Bay.","wpu":"Kobe","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/20190901_Kobe_harbor-1.jpg/960px-20190901_Kobe_harbor-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Kobe Doll Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":34.6894,"lo":135.190576,"d":713,"h":"10:00-18:00","w":"https://timeroman.com/kobedollmuseum/","ph":"+81 78 327 4680","wp":"ja:神戸ドールミュージアム"},{"n":"Monument of the memorial and reconstruction","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":34.687475,"lo":135.197029,"d":812},{"n":"Kobe Harborland","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":34.678512,"lo":135.180311,"d":1016,"wp":"en:Harborland","ds":"Harborland (神戸ハーバーランド, kōbe-hābārando) is a shopping district in Chuo-ku, Kobe, Japan. Kobe Port Tower is located there. This shopping district was made on the site of the former freight yard, Minatogawa Kamotsu Station of the Japanese National Railways.","wpu":"Harborland","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Harborland_district.jpg/960px-Harborland_district.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"D51 1072 Locomotive","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":34.681233,"lo":135.178813,"d":1041},{"n":"神戸港駅の記憶","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":34.687032,"lo":135.200337,"d":1046},{"n":"防火水そう","g":"sights","k":"archaeological_site","la":34.679784,"lo":135.1788,"d":1084},{"n":"浣心亭","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":34.692137,"lo":135.181785,"d":1263},{"n":"Funa-Yakata Pleasure Barge","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":34.692119,"lo":135.181412,"d":1282,"wp":"ja:船屋形"},{"n":"Treasure House","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":34.680689,"lo":135.175891,"d":1315},{"n":"旧相楽園会館","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":34.692737,"lo":135.181191,"d":1349},{"n":"旧ハッサム住宅","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":34.693076,"lo":135.181592,"d":1358,"wp":"ja:旧ハッサム住宅"},{"n":"Kobe Kaigan Dori Post Office","g":"essentials","k":"post_office","la":34.686461,"lo":135.187505,"d":447,"h":"Mo-Fr 09:00-17:00","ph":"+81-78-391-0131"},{"n":"ATM","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":34.68832,"lo":135.191978,"d":618},{"n":"OS Drug","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":34.688573,"lo":135.18833,"d":638,"h":"Mo-Su 09:30-19:15"},{"n":"Matsukiyo","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":34.688722,"lo":135.189212,"d":640},{"n":"Kokokara Fine","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":34.687623,"lo":135.185488,"d":659},{"n":"KALDI","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":34.687898,"lo":135.185558,"d":679},{"n":"Kobe Motomachi Post Office","g":"essentials","k":"post_office","la":34.689